Z||000000||pHoOl||12-24-2000||01:26 AM||||With regards to your scoop, how much of a difference does it make in performance?  I'm looking for something cheap to add on to give me an extra push.  Talked to someone who said that they can feel the air flow with their hang getting sucked onto the scoop, but i'd like to know if you can feel it when hitting the gas peddle.<P>lemme know, and we'll have to get all of us michigan people together to cruise<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||12-24-2000||01:34 AM||||If you really want to find out how well they work without buying one. Make one out of a 1 liter bottle and some duct tape.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||12-24-2000||03:19 PM||||Don't have any test results or dyno numbers  to compare yet.  However, one thing I've found with my Fiero is that it seems to have more throttle response on the highway than without it.  We noticed the same on John's Fiero and a few people with them also told us the same.<P>Overall we designed it to look cool, any functionality that it does add is a plus.<P>Cruises would be cool!  Doing some work on my Fiero over the winter, definitely can't wait for spring.<P>Happy Holidays!<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue3.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||MachineHead||12-24-2000||04:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>If you really want to find out how well they work without buying one. Make one out of a 1 liter bottle and some duct tape.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Or since it is Christmas, use a wrapping paper roll, one of the big ones.  They ought to be plentiful. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||12-24-2000||10:51 PM||||The real question here was directed for me.<P>I don't think pHoOl was asking for paper or plastic?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||pHoOl||12-24-2000||11:19 PM||||Alright, i know how a scoop works, but what would i use to elbow it into the duct if i was going to take a 20oz or something?  i figured that there must be something to attach.  heehee<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||12-25-2000||12:49 AM||||Tigger, I know it was directed to you. I also knew that you didn't have any performance numbers on it. I was just making a suggestion to let him see for himself if there was an increase.<P>First, take the louvered grille off the inlet. Then cut the bottle then trim the bottle to fit onto the louvers like a scoop and attach with the duct tape. You'll have to make holes in the scoop to get a screwdriver into. It will look really stupid so drive at night.||||reg||1
